## Tracking

Unit and integration: the number of cases of the suite named after the class, then, for integration, the
tests that check the class through another suite. *Remarks* name the rows of
[Known Architectural Debt](../Architecture.md#known-architectural-debt) that concern the class; no class
of `Core` declares a test as a friend (the friend test of that table is in `Parser::FMTParser`). *Status*
is the lot that plans its unit tests (section 6.3 of the ETAT).

| Priority | Header | Class | Unit | Integration | System tests with a check | Known issues | Remarks | Status |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
@TRACKING_ROWS@
## Description

The other columns of #350. *Build options* are the conditional compilations found in the header and its
source: FMT is built with MSVC and with MSYS2 only, and the portability that #350 asks for is lot 9.
*To assess (lot 9)* marks a question that lot 9 answers: thread safety and allocations are measured
there, not guessed here.

| Class | Source file | Public operations | External dependencies | Build options | Serialization | Thread safety | Allocation-sensitive | Missing tests |
